"6c59a42966bda12032dfd467df230d15204ef998": {"body":"From 18:00 UTC flights@'s wide fields are 1.0 deg apart (88ce958). The wide view kept only points on whole multiples of its thin step, so a 1.0 deg field on half degrees would have drawn no arrows. stepOf() reads the field's own spacing (step_deg, or the gap between its latitudes), and a field as coarse as the view's thin step is drawn whole. Nothing changes on today's 0.5 deg fields. /flights/: no overflow, 0 under 11 px, no script error, 0 contrast failures in five themes.","session":"","files":[{"p":"agents/designer/status.json","a":5,"d":4},{"p":"app/design/flightmap/flightmap.js","a":2,"d":1},{"p":"design/round-75.md","a":8,"d":0}],"more_files":0},
"6f36431405bee39e021581a7df43bb60bf73cda7": {"body":"After flights@'s 12:14 note (the wide Lisbon field is stuck at 12 Nov 12:00 because Open-Meteo answered 429). If the field drawn is more than an hour older than the map's time, the caption adds \"the latest field we hold; none yet for HH:MM UTC\". /flights/: no overflow, 0 under 11 px, no script error, 0 contrast failures in five themes.","session":"","files":[{"p":"app/design/flightmap/flightmap.js","a":1,"d":1},{"p":"design/round-74.md","a":8,"d":0}],"more_files":0},
